# Bastion's leaders, the hub (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Hubs: work comes out of talk"): 0 the job, 1 the
# built news, 2 what they make of you, each carried by a topic. Voice: clipped, procedural, tired;
# close with its own. Nobody is coming. Bastion lies by leaving things out.
# Work talk explains the work (what, where, who for, the pay, the danger) before the accept.

conv bastion.leader.work_wire
for stronghold:bastion, seat:bastion/outpost_lead
when need:security
topic "What does the map table say?"
prio ask
voice bastion

bind over = news:overrun
bind horde = news:horde

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? stronghold :: This is the map table. Red pins are them, blue pins are us, and there's less blue than last week. Every post in the Zone reports into this table at twenty hundred.
  say? trait:paranoid :: Close the door first. Who saw you come in? Fine. The map, then. Red pins are them, blue are us. I trust the pins more than I trust most people.
  say The map says we're thin. Three posts' worth of ground covered by men for two. Every gap between our pins is a road the infected can walk down to somebody's door.
  say? bound:horde :: A crowd of them moved near {bind:horde} overnight. Somebody ran an engine or rang something, and they came to look. They always come to look.
  say? bound:over :: {bind:over} is lost to them. Contact on the south side at dusk, then silence on the net. We pulled the pin this morning.
  say? night :: Night watch is set. Half of them have been on since oh-five-thirty, and you can hear it on the net.
  say Our order is to hold what we hold. Command gave it on Day 2 and never took it back, so it's ours now.
  > @where Where's the line weakest? -> weak
  > @command What does Command say about it? -> command
  > @pay What does Bastion pay? -> pay
  > @soldier Show me the duty rota. -> rota   if bg:soldier,police
  > @help Is there something I can do? -> offer
  > @no Not today. -> hub

node weak
  say? bound:over :: Between here and {bind:over}. There's nothing between us and that town now but a ditch and a sign we painted ourselves.
  say Wherever we aren't. That's the honest answer, and it's always the answer. The infected don't attack a post. They walk round it to whatever's soft.
  say The houses are soft. The Haven's people come to our wire when it goes bad, and some nights I've nobody to send back with them.
  > @help2 Then send me where you aren't. -> offer
  > @back1 I'll keep that in mind. -> hub

node command
  say Command says nothing. We call at oh-six-hundred and twenty hundred. Static both times, and the operator logs it like a reply.
  say? trait:veteran :: Sergeant Holt used to answer for Command at the north post, in the voice. Very good impression. He's in the ground outside that post now, and nobody does the voice.
  say So the orders come from this table now. Somebody had to give them, and nobody else volunteered.
  > @help3 Then I'll take an order from you. -> offer
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node pay
  say? trait:greedy :: Pay first, then the job. Fine. Rations, Favor with our quartermaster, and a line in the log. Don't sneer at the line. The log decides who we go looking for.
  say Favor with our quartermaster, rations from our stores, ammunition if it's that kind of job, and your name in the log. The log is who we feed and who we go looking for.
  say? !tier:bastion>=known :: Do enough of it and the sentries stop searching you at our checkpoints. That alone saves you an hour a day.
  > @help4 That'll do. What's the job? -> offer
  > @back3 Let me think about it. Something else. -> hub

node rota
  say Here. Twelve names on this post's rota. Four of them are dead and still on it, because taking them off would make the gap real, and then somebody would have to stand in it.
  say You read a rota like a rota. Good. Most civilians read it as a list of people.
  do learn:bastion.rota_dead:6h
  > @help5 Then put me in one of the gaps. -> offer
  > @back4 Noted. Something else. -> hub

node offer
  say Here's how it works. I give you a task off this table: a town to clear, a patrol to find, a road to watch, a checkpoint to hold. You do it, you report to any post.
  say It pays in Favor and rations and a line in the log. It's dangerous: every pin on this table is there because something went wrong.
  say? tier:bastion>=trusted :: You're on the roster already, under civilians attached, so you get the same tasking the soldiers get.
  > @take I'll do it. Give me the task. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @risk How bad does it get out there? -> risk
  > @later Not yet. Let me think on it. -> hub

node risk
  say Last week a patrol of four went to look at a pharmacy and two came back. The report says contact, withdrew. The two who came back don't say anything.
  say I don't send civilians where I wouldn't send my own. But I send my own everywhere, so read that how you like.
  > @take4 Understood. I'll do it. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later4 Then not today. -> hub

node other_route
  say You've committed to another outfit's route for the cure. Noted, and logged. You won't hear the in-jokes from us for a while.
  say We still have gaps on this table, and you still have hands. Tasking pays the same whoever you march with.
  > @take2 Then I'll take a task anyway. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node after
  say? cure_held:bastion :: We hold the cure. Orders are to issue it by name and signature. Orders are also to stand the line down. We're doing both, badly.
  say The cure's out and the line is standing down. Processing at the road checkpoints, they say. The barriers are still closed.
  say We still have names on the board that nobody's found. I'd like them found before anyone walks out at the north road.
  > @take3 Then give me a name to find. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv bastion.leader.work
for stronghold:bastion, seat:bastion/outpost_lead
when !need:security
topic "What needs doing at the wire?"
prio ask
voice bastion

bind truck = supply:truck
bind short = supply:short

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? need:food :: Rations. We're down to the brown packets at the back of the store. Nobody knows what's in the brown packets, and the quartermaster won't guess.
  say? need:supplies :: Supplies. Ammunition, mask filters, batteries. We count rounds at the roll now, same as names, and both numbers are going the wrong way.
  say? need:people :: People. Live ones who can stand a watch. We've more posts than men to put on them, and the men we have haven't slept.
  say? need:revenge :: Somebody shot one of ours. Bastion doesn't ask who started it. It keeps a list and it sends people, and right now the list is longer than the people.
  say Same as yesterday. Hold the post, watch the road, log what moves, get the trucks through. Nothing comes from outside, so everything we eat came down one of our roads.
  say? supply:short & bound:short :: {bind:short} is short and the truck's late. Late is a word we use. It means nothing is coming until somebody goes and gets it.
  say? rain :: And it's raining, which is the one thing round here nobody had to order.
  say? fog :: And there's fog. Fog is when the drones over the line see nothing and we see less.
  > @truck Where's the truck headed? -> truck   if supply:road
  > @why Why are you still holding here? -> why
  > @press What's the report leaving out? -> told | short_said | short_said   check persuade bastion 2 harder:paranoid bg:soldier,police
  > @help What can I do for you? -> offer
  > @no Not today. -> hub

node truck
  say It's on the road to {bind:truck}. Two men, one rifle, one radio, and whatever's in the back that we can't spare.
  say Don't follow it. If you follow it, so will they, and so will the Red Hand. Their crews know our trucks by the sound.
  > @help2 I could ride along with it. -> offer
  > @back1 I'll stay clear of it. -> hub

node why
  say? trait:idealist :: Because somebody has to be where the government said it would be. We're the government now. That's the whole joke, and I've stopped laughing at it.
  say The order on Day 2 was hold the line and await relief. Nobody countermanded it. So we hold.
  say And because when it goes bad, the people in the houses come to the wire. Somebody has to be standing at the wire when they get here.
  > @help3 Then let me help hold it. -> offer
  > @back2 Fair enough. Something else. -> hub

node told
  say? supply:lost :: We lost a truck. The crew walked in. The cargo didn't. The report says delayed, and delayed is accurate until somebody asks how long.
  say Last patrol came back one short. The report says the patrol saw nothing. That's correct. The man who isn't here saw something, and he isn't here to log it.
  do learn:bastion.report_short:6h
  > @help4 Then send me where he went. -> offer
  > @back3 I'm sorry. Something else. -> hub

node short_said
  say The report is accurate. It's in the log. You can read the log when you're in the log, and you get in the log by doing tasks for this post.
  > @help5 Then put me in the log. -> offer
  > @back4 Another time, then. -> hub

node offer
  say? trait:ruthless :: There's work. The form was short, so's the briefing: a place, a task, a time to report back. You'll get all three.
  say There's tasking. Escorting a truck, clearing a road, finding a patrol that missed its call, standing a checkpoint. Whatever it is, you report back to a Bastion post when it's done.
  say It pays Favor with our quartermaster and rations, and it goes in the log under your name. Some of it gets people shot. Listen to all of it before you say yes.
  > @take I'm in. Give me the task. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later Not yet. -> hub

node other_route
  say You've committed to another outfit's route for the cure. Noted, and logged. You won't hear the in-jokes from us for a while.
  say The wire still needs holding, and you still have hands. Tasking pays the same whoever you march with.
  > @take2 Then I'll take a task anyway. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node after
  say The line is standing down. Drones gone home, loudspeakers on a new tape. The barriers are still closed.
  say There's still a road full of people who don't believe any of it, and somebody in a uniform has to stand on that road and be calm.
  > @take3 Then give me something to do. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 Let me ask something else. -> hub

# Bastion's word on a post it lost: it was a withdrawal (a lie by leaving out), until somebody who
# saw it tells you otherwise (posts and other factions' people, ~truth:gossip.withdrew@lost).
conv bastion.leader.news
for stronghold:bastion, seat:bastion/outpost_lead
topic "What's in the morning report?"
prio world
voice bastion

bind lost = news:lost_by(bastion)
bind took = news:taken
bind who = news:taken_by
bind dead = news:leader_dead
bind horde = news:horde
bind shelled = news:shelled

node start
  jump news:lost_by(bastion) -> lost
  jump news:leader_dead -> dead
  jump news:shelled -> shelled
  jump news:taken -> taken
  jump news:horde -> horde
  say? stand :: Report: the lab is under attack and every outfit in the Zone wants what's inside it. We hold our posts. Holding is what we do.
  say? epilogue :: Report: the line stood down. Processing at the road checkpoints. Nobody believes processing, and nobody's wrong yet.
  say? edge :: Report: drones over the line, as usual. Loudspeakers, as usual. Nobody crossed. Nobody crosses. We log it anyway.
  say? cure>=75 :: Report: the lab's past seventy-five percent. Command was informed at twenty hundred. Command was silent at twenty hundred.
  say Report: no contact worth the name. Night watch saw lights to the east and logged them. Lights to the east are a report, so we report them.
  say? night :: It's not morning. You get the night report, which is shorter and worse.
  > @mine What's in the log about me? -> me
  > @more Anything else come in on the net? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back0 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node lost
  say We withdrew from {bind:lost}. Orderly. Equipment recovered. Casualties within tolerance. ~lie:gossip.withdrew@lost
  say Tolerance is a word we use now. It used to mean something about engines.
  > @catch Withdrew? I heard you were thrown out. -> caught   callout gossip.withdrew@lost
  > @more1 What else came in on the net? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node caught
  say Thrown out. Yes. Correct. The report will say withdrew. The men who were there will say the other thing, and they'll be right.
  say I'd rather you heard it from me. Now you have. Don't repeat it at the wire. They've had enough of hearing it.
  > @more2 What else came in on the net? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back2 I won't. Something else. -> hub

node dead
  say {bind:dead}, deceased. Confirmed by two sources. One was a radio. The other was a patrol that went to look.
  say? trait:veteran :: We'll read the name at the roll tonight. We read everyone's, even the ones who weren't ours. It costs nothing but breath.
  say Somebody will fill that chair. Somebody always fills the chair. That's the trouble with chairs.
  > @more3 What else came in on the net? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back3 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node shelled
  say Fire mission near {bind:shelled}. Ours. Authorised. I won't say by whom, and I won't say it was wise.
  say Four shells on a crowd of them. The crowd's gone. So is the street they were standing in.
  > @more4 What else came in on the net? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back4 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node taken
  say {bind:who} has {bind:took}. Logged, and the map's updated. Pins are cheap. Getting a town back isn't.
  say? feud:redhand :: If it's the Red Hand, there'll be a toll on the road out of it by supper. That's not a guess. That's a pattern.
  > @more5 What else came in on the net? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node horde
  say Large contact near {bind:horde}, moving with the noise. We don't engage crowds. We let them walk past and write them down.
  say If you're headed that way, go quiet: no engines, no shots you don't need. They come to sound like we come to a radio.
  > @more6 What else came in on the net? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back6 I'll go quiet. Something else. -> hub

node me
  jump kit:other -> me_colours
  say? kit:own :: Attached personnel. Kit correctly worn, mostly. The collar was noted.
  say? kills:bastion>=2 :: Your name's in the log next to ours. Not in the good column. Every one of them is still on a board somewhere.
  say? best:bastion :: Entry: you {best}. Underlined. We don't underline much.
  say Civilian. Seen at the wire. No further entries. That's a clean page. Keep it that way, or don't.
  > @back7 Fair enough. Something else. -> hub

node me_colours
  say Entry: civilian at the wire in another outfit's colours. Possibly a thief. Possibly cold. Logged as both until I know which.
  > @back8 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv bastion.leader.me
for stronghold:bastion, seat:bastion/outpost_lead
topic "How would you log me?"
prio reaction
voice bastion

node start
  jump kit:other -> colours
  jump bite_shown -> bitten
  jump kills:bastion>=2 -> killer
  jump tier:bastion>=trusted -> trusted
  jump tier:bastion>=known -> known
  say? fresh :: New arrival. No history. History is what we write after you've done something, and you haven't yet.
  say Civilian. Unattached. Not a threat at this time. The at this time is doing a lot of work in that sentence.
  > @more And in full? Where do I stand with you? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @fair Understood. -> hub

node colours
  say? kit:issued :: That jacket is ours. It was signed out to somebody, and you're not the name on the sheet.
  say You're in someone else's colours at my wire. That goes in the log before your name does, and the sentries read the log.
  > @more1 And under my name? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node bitten
  say Bite on the arm. I'm logging it. I hope you're getting it declared at the nearest house, or walking to the lab for the trial dose.
  say We don't shoot the bitten. We watch them, and somebody sits with them at the end. Don't make the watching interesting.
  > @more2 Am I still cleared at your wire? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back2 I'll get it seen to. -> hub

node killer
  say You've put {kills} of ours in the ground. Each one is a name we read at the roll. Each one is still on the board.
  say I'm talking to you because standing orders say talk first. Standing orders are getting old.
  > @more3 Then say it. Where do I stand? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back3 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node trusted
  say? title:bastion :: The men call you {title:bastion}. They don't name civilians. Draw your own conclusion.
  say? best:bastion :: You {best}. It's on the board, under ours.
  say You're on the roster, under civilians attached. We go looking for the people on the roster. That's not a courtesy. It's the rule.
  > @more4 Where do I stand, in full? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back4 Thank you. Something else. -> hub

node known
  say? jobs:bastion>=3 :: Three tasks or more, completed and logged. That's a pattern. We like patterns.
  say Known at the wire. The sentries won't ask your name twice. They'll still ask once, and they'll still search the bag.
  > @more5 And where do I stand overall? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub
